 "result": "The default session serializer is `TypedCookieSerializer`, which tags non-JSON types on the way out and untags them on the way in.\n\n- **`TypedCookieSerializer`** (`src/tessel/json/tag.py:219`): `dumps` (321) calls `tag` (289) to wrap values before JSON encoding. `loads` (325) calls `untag` (297) to restore the original types.\n- **`TypeMarker`** (`src/tessel/json/tag.py:60`): the base class for the per-type markers. Each marker checks whether it matches a value, converts it to a JSON-safe form with a one-letter key, and converts it back.\n  - **Tuples**: `TagTuple` (133) stores them as lists under a `\" t\"` key. `PassList` (147) leaves ordinary lists alone.\n  - **Bytes**: `TagBytes` (159) base64-encodes them.\n  - **Datetimes**: `TagDateTime` (205) stores them as HTTP-date strings.\n  - **Also handled**: `TagUUID` (191), `TagMarkup` (173), and `TagDict` (93, escapes dicts that look like tagged ones).\n- **`session_json_serializer`** (`src/tessel/sessions.py:273`): the module-level `TypedCookieSerializer()` instance.\n- **`SignedCookieSessionInterface`** (`src/tessel/sessions.py:284`): sets `serializer = session_json_serializer` (300) and passes it to the signing serializer (316), so the cookie is signed JSON with these tags.",
